			<abstract>
				<p>In this paper, kinematics modelling of a 3 degree-of-freedom (DOF) planar PRP (P-Prismatic, R-Revolute, P-Prismatic) parallel manipulator is presented. By solving the inverse kinematics, position and velocity of actuators in terms of position and velocity of end-effector are expressed. Secondly, considering various non-dimensional performance measures, namely, WSI, GCI and GSI as the objective functions, a multi-objective optimization problem is formulated. Finally, optimal solution is obtained using Genetic Algorithms (GA). Effect of tool platform orientation angle (θ) on the performance indices is also studied.</p>
			</abstract>
